Louver's code before the motherboard RGB port (commit d5b59b1 and earlier) was
MIT-licensed; from this release on, Louver is GPL-2.0-or-later.

Louver is written in Python. Its Lian Li drivers (louver/devices.py) follow
the Rust implementation in lian-li-linux, and its unverified effect numbers
come from it; the controller protocol was also cross-checked against
uni-sync, which shares no code with Louver. lian-li-linux's MIT notice
below still applies to the parts of louver/devices.py that follow it.

  lian-li-linux  https://github.com/sgtaziz/lian-li-linux
                 Copyright (c) 2026 sgtaziz, MIT License (full notice below)
  uni-sync       https://github.com/EightB1ts/uni-sync
                 Copyright (c) 2023 Cameron Halter, MIT License

Its ASUS Aura driver (louver/aura.py) is a port to Python of OpenRGB's Aura
USB mainboard driver, GNU GPL version 2 or (at your option) any later
version, at commit b190d3e5afb6bd68b4bfa3e948947878d2bf1ba9:

  OpenRGB        https://gitlab.com/CalcProgrammer1/OpenRGB
                 Controllers/AsusAuraUSBController/
                   AsusAuraUSBController/AsusAuraUSBController.h, .cpp (Martin Hartl):
                     the firmware and config-table queries
                   AsusAuraUSBController/AsusAuraMainboardController.h, .cpp (Martin Hartl):
                     the channels, effect and effect-colour commands
                   AsusAuraUSBController/RGBController_AsusAuraUSB.cpp (Adam Honse):
                     the effect list
                   AsusAuraUSBControllerDetect.cpp: the mainboard product IDs
                 Not ported: the save-to-device commit (it writes the
                 controller's flash) and direct per-LED mode.

